=== Prompt ===
Who is Ellie from The Last of Us?

=== Response ===
Ellie, full name Ellie Rose Abbott, is one of the main characters in the post-apocalyptic action-adventure video game series "The Last of Us" and its sequel, developed by Naughty Dog and published by Sony Interactive Entertainment. She was voiced by Ashley Johnson in the games.

In the story, Ellie is a young survivor living in a world ravaged by a fungal infection called Cordyceps that has turned most of humanity into zombie-like creatures called Infected. She is 15 years old when the game begins, and she is a friend and companion to Joel, who takes her under his wing after she is orphaned.

Throughout the game and the sequel, Ellie's character evolves significantly. She is intelligent, resourceful, and determined, with a strong moral compass. She becomes an important figure in the resistance against the infected and other survivors. Her journey involves growth, personal development, and complex relationships with other characters, particularly Joel, leading to significant emotional moments and plot developments.

In the sequel, "The Last of Us Part II," Ellie plays a crucial role as a leader in the Sodden resistance, leading a group of survivors and working towards a better future. The game explores her past, her motivations, and the consequences of her actions, making her one of the most compelling and deeply developed characters in modern gaming.

